            "\"Together [Jim and his father] crossed the\nlawn towards the flower-bed. At some\nyards from the broken peony Jimmie\nbegan to lag. 'There!' The word came\n[from Jim] almost breathlessly.\"",
            "\"Little Jim was, for the time, engine\nNumber 36, and he was making the run\nbetween Syracuse and Rochester. He was\nfourteen minutes behind time, and the\nthrottle was wide open.\"",
