          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 6 · Q64",
          "passageTitle": "Quotation — Q64",
          "passage": "Cane is a 1923 novel by Jean Toomer. In one\nportion of the novel, Toomer uses figurative\nlanguage to connect the narrator's urban\nenvironment of Washington, DC, and the rural\nSouth of the narrator's past, writing,",
          "prompt": "Which quotation from Cane most effectively\nillustrates the claim?",
