          "passageTitle": "Quotation — Q70",
          "passage": "Uncle Vanya: Scenes from Country Life in Four\nActs is an 1898 play by Anton Chekhov,\noriginally written in Russian. In the play,\nProfessor Serebrakoff and his wife Helena have\ncome to stay at their country estate, which\nVanya manages with the help of Sonia, the\nprofessor's daughter from a previous marriage.\nChekhov portrays the relationship between\nVanya and Professor Serebrakoff as being much\nmore strained than it once was, as is evident\nwhen",
